```java
// @OneToMany — Order has many Items
@Entity
public class Order {
    @Id private Long id;

    @OneToMany(mappedBy = "order", cascade = CascadeType.ALL)
    private List<OrderItem> items = new ArrayList<>();
}

// @ManyToOne — Item belongs to Order
@Entity
public class OrderItem {
    @Id private Long id;

    @ManyToOne(fetch = FetchType.LAZY)
    @JoinColumn(name = "order_id")  // FK column
    private Order order;
}
```

In a **bidirectional** relationship, both sides need references to each other in Java. But at the database level, there's only ONE foreign key column. JPA needs to know which side 'owns' the FK.

- **Owning side**: has `@JoinColumn` — controls the FK
- **Inverse side**: has `mappedBy` — just for navigation in Java, no DB column

```java
// Owning side — has the FK in its table
@ManyToOne
@JoinColumn(name = "order_id")  // FK column: order_id in order_item table
private Order order;

// Inverse side — no FK, just back-reference
@OneToMany(mappedBy = "order")  // references the 'order' field above
private List<OrderItem> items;
```

```java
// Cascade PERSIST and MERGE — safe for most relationships
@OneToMany(mappedBy = "order",
           cascade = {CascadeType.PERSIST, CascadeType.MERGE})
private List<OrderItem> items;

// Cascade ALL — parent owns child lifecycle completely
@OneToOne(cascade = CascadeType.ALL, orphanRemoval = true)
private UserProfile profile;  // profile deleted when user deleted
```

**Common usage**: `CascadeType.PERSIST` — saving parent also saves new children. `CascadeType.REMOVE` — deleting parent also deletes children (use with `orphanRemoval=true`).

```java
@Entity
public class Student {
    @Id private Long id;
    private String name;

    @ManyToMany  // owning side — controls join table
    @JoinTable(
        name = "student_course",
        joinColumns = @JoinColumn(name = "student_id"),
        inverseJoinColumns = @JoinColumn(name = "course_id")
    )
    private Set<Course> courses = new HashSet<>();
}

@Entity
public class Course {
    @Id private Long id;
    private String title;

    @ManyToMany(mappedBy = "courses")  // inverse side
    private Set<Student> students = new HashSet<>();
}
```
